// Reactivity S3 — `computed(fn)` is lazy and memoized. Its body runs on *read*, not on creation, and
// only when a dependency it read has changed; a read with no intervening change returns the memo
// without recomputing. The body echoes "computing" each time it actually runs, so the output witnesses
// exactly when a recompute happens: once on the first `.get()`, skipped on the immediate second
// `.get()` (memoized), and once more after `count.set(3)` dirties it. This laziness + memoization is
// the whole point of `computed` over a plain function call.
// expect: stdout "start"
// expect: stdout "computing"
// expect: stdout "doubled=4"
// expect: stdout "doubled=4"
// expect: stdout "computing"
// expect: stdout "doubled=6"
// expect: exit 0
count = signal(2)
doubled = computed(fn() { echo "computing"; return count.get() * 2 })
echo "start"
echo "doubled=${doubled.get()}"
echo "doubled=${doubled.get()}"
count.set(3)
echo "doubled=${doubled.get()}"
